# {{.project_name}}

Production-shaped iOS app generated by smokeforge.

## Requirements

- macOS with Xcode 26.6 or later
- XcodeGen 2.48.0
- iOS 17 minimum deployment target

This template is authored and validated on macOS CI. It does not include a
committed `.xcodeproj`; `project.yml` is the source of truth.

## Commands

```bash
make project   # generate the Xcode project
make test      # run Swift package tests
make build     # build for the iOS Simulator
make ci
```

## Stack

- Swift 6 with strict concurrency
- SwiftUI, Observation, NavigationStack
- Local Swift packages for Core, Networking, Storage, Data, DesignSystem, and features
- URLSession async/await
- Keychain token storage
- Swift Testing
- XcodeGen 2.48.0

## Behaviour

- Email/password login, registration, password-reset request, refresh rotation,
  logout, and current-account loading against the smokeforge API.
- Access and refresh tokens live in Keychain with a device-only accessibility
  class.
- Debug, Staging, and Release configurations use separate xcconfig files.
- Debug API default: `http://127.0.0.1:8080` for the simulator.
- No SwiftData, offline sync, OAuth, TOTP, analytics, or crash reporting in the
  base.

## Layout

```text
App/                    @main app, container, root coordinator, assets
Packages/Core/          pure models, errors, protocols, theme preference
Packages/Networking/    URLSession API client and problem details
Packages/Storage/       Keychain token store
Packages/Data/          repositories and session policy
Packages/DesignSystem/  Smoke theme and shared SwiftUI components
Packages/TestSupport/   fakes and fixtures
Packages/AuthFeature/   auth screens and ViewModel
Packages/HomeFeature/   API status and account summary
Packages/SettingsFeature/ appearance and sign-out
Config/                 Debug/Staging/Release xcconfigs
docs/                   architecture, auth, networking, storage, testing, release
```

Read `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTEXT.md`, and `DESIGN.md` before changing
code. Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for the dependency direction.
